"""Plain-English metric help shared by the offline report views."""

METRIC_HELP = {
    "Evaluable case coverage": "Evaluable cases / planned cases × 100. Quota, context and execution blocks do not count as evaluable. In the matched cohort, the denominator is the common cases.",
    "Complete conversations": "Conversations with final status complete / evaluable conversations × 100. Evaluable failures stay in the denominator; infrastructure blocks do not.",
    "Ordered flow milestones": "Conversations whose recorded node path contains every expected milestone in order / evaluable conversations with an expected path × 100. Extra steps are allowed; repeated milestones must still occur.",
    "Expected tools": "Passed positive tool expectations / all applicable positive expectations × 100, including unreached turns. Checks require a native function call with the expected name, schema-valid arguments matching the configured subset, count and turn. Saying a tool will be called is insufficient. Backend responses are mocked.",
    "Explicit case rules": "Passed programmed assertions / applicable assertions × 100. Checks cover configured required/forbidden text, word limits, active nodes, forbidden tools, tool counts and tool-before-text order. This is not a semantic assessment of every instruction in a prompt.",
    "TTFT": "Seconds from API request start to the first streamed text or tool-call delta. Reasoning-only deltas do not stop this timer. This is the benchmark's operational TTFT definition, measured by the client; it is not necessarily text a user can see.",
    "Full latency": "Seconds from API request start until that response stream finishes. Includes the provider's processing and the network time observed by the client. This measures one API call, not the entire conversation.",
    "First native tool delta": "Seconds from API request start to the first native tool-call delta. Only calls with a recorded native tool delta contribute; textual tool emulation is excluded.",
    "First user-facing text": "Seconds from the start of a simulated user turn until its first visible assistant text. Includes preceding LLM calls, orchestration and mock tool steps in that turn. No visible text means a missing sample, not zero. Local quota waits are subtracted. This does not measure synthesized audio.",
    "Flow latency": "Seconds to finish one simulated user turn across all of its LLM calls, orchestration, transitions and mock tool results. Local quota waits are subtracted. This is per turn, not the sum of the whole conversation, and excludes speech recognition and synthesis.",
    "Native function calls": "Count of native structured function calls emitted per evaluable conversation. An attempted call counts even though the backend is mocked. Textual promises and emulated calls are excluded.",
    "Invalid function calls": "Count of tool calls rejected by the configured tool contract, for example an unknown function or invalid arguments, per evaluable conversation. It is not a real backend failure rate.",
    "Confirmed language flags": "Number of flagged text fragments reviewed and confirmed as outside the configured allowed language policy, per evaluable conversation. This depends on detection and review; zero flags does not prove zero language leakage.",
    "Pending language flags": "Number of detected language flags still awaiting review, per evaluable conversation. They are not confirmed errors. Reviewed false positives are excluded from both confirmed and pending counts.",
    "Accepted input size": "Input tokens reported by the provider for accepted calls, including recorded portions of incomplete conversations. This shows observed request sizes; it does not prove the model used all context correctly or establish its maximum context capacity.",
    "Reasoning tokens": "Reasoning-token count recorded from provider usage on accepted calls. Interpretation and reporting depend on the provider; zero alone does not prove thinking was disabled. Compare the recorded reasoning profiles too.",
    "Known cost per API call": "Calculated USD per recorded call with known cost, including calls in incomplete conversations. Formula: ((input − cached input) × input rate + cached input × cache-read rate + billable output × output rate) / 1,000,000. Reasoning is added only when not already included in output usage. Missing cache rates use the input rate. Unknown costs are excluded, not assumed free; this is not an invoice.",
    "Known cost per conversation": "Sum of call costs for a recorded conversation, included only when it has calls and every call cost is known. Incomplete conversations can contribute their recorded costs. Not a total campaign cost or an invoice.",
    "Quota wait": "Local time spent waiting for the configured provider quota before recorded API calls. Shown separately and excluded from response/turn latency measurements. This does not remove provider-side queueing from measured latency.",
    "Infrastructure block rate": "Recorded cases blocked by execution, quota or context errors / recorded cases × 100. These blocks are tracked separately from model-quality failures. Unrun combinations are not in this denominator.",
    "Scenario status": "Recorded outcome for this model and simulated scenario. Complete, evaluable quality failures, infrastructure blocks and unrun combinations remain distinct.",
    "Total known cost": "Sum of known call costs for this model in the selected scope, including recorded incomplete attempts in that selection. This is a total, not a per-call price. Unknown costs are not treated as verified zero; earlier runs outside this selection are not included.",
    "Largest accepted input": "Maximum provider-reported input token count among accepted calls in this selection. This is an observed request size, not a guarantee about maximum context or context-following quality.",
    "Native / invalid function calls": "Totals of native function calls and contract-invalid calls in the selected scope. Tool backends are simulated. These are counts, not a success percentage.",
    "Language flags: confirmed / pending": "Counts of reviewed foreign-language fragments and flags awaiting review in this selection. False positives are excluded. No flags does not guarantee no language leakage.",
    "Provider or context rejections": "Number of recorded execution, quota or context blocks in the selection. These are reported separately and are not scored as model-quality failures.",
}
